;; lei-candidates.edn — acquisition work list for the cloud-itonami-lei catalog.
;;
;; Adding a company is adding ONE map to this vector. Nothing else in the
;; pipeline needs to change: scripts/lei-acquire.cljs verifies every entry
;; against GLEIF, so a wrong name or a wrong country here fails loudly as a
;; lookup miss rather than entering the catalog unverified.
;;
;; :name    the entity's LEGAL name as registered, not its brand. GLEIF is
;;          searched by legal name + jurisdiction, and a brand ("Google")
;;          usually is not the registered name ("Alphabet Inc.").
;; :country ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, matched against GLEIF's own jurisdiction.
;; :site    candidate official website. VERIFIED before use -- the fetched page
;;          must actually mention the company -- so a stale or wrong guess here
;;          is recorded as unverified rather than published as fact.
;;
;; Selection for this pass: the countries the catalog had ZERO coverage of
;; after the 2026-07-25 normalisation showed real coverage was 27 countries
;; (US alone 55%), not the 53 that the un-normalised jurisdiction strings
;; suggested. National champions / largest listed issuers per country, since
;; those are the entities most likely to have both a real LEI and a published
;; legal/privacy page.

